2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1057) '**The dev container.** RFD66606-1056. The image does not build yet. The Debian attempt failed at `mix local.hex`, and the Fedora rewrite answers that by reading the error. Build it before trusting it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1057  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1057) '**The Pixal3D worker stage.** RFD66606-1040. Only the contract stage ran. The worker stage pulls 24.045 GB and needs an NVIDIA device, thus it needs a rented card.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1057  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1057) '**The local worker.** RFD66606-1055 Phase 2. No worker service runs on this box yet, only a manual contract-stage test (RFD66606-1040). No instance is rented either, and RFD66606-1062's Gall's law says none should be, until this box is not enough.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1057  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1057) '**The Fly.io / 4090 split.** RFD66606-1062. No `fly.toml`, no worker-side job-receiving adapter, no Tailscale join between a Fly machine and this box, no CockroachDB migration off this box. RFD66606-1062 names the target. None of it runs yet. The adapter's asset-transport half is settled, `idtx_transport`/aria-storage, per RFD66606-1062's own DETAILS.md. Open work narrows to the job-control envelope, and whether an aria-storage instance runs anywhere reachable yet.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1057  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1057) 'Measured, and not built
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1057  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1057) '**Fourteen model folders.** RFD66606-1036. Each still carries a `cog.yaml` and a `predict.py`, and RFD66606-1036 no longer selects Cog. Convert one when its model is next worked on, and not in a sweep. The folder names are already converted, and the files inside are not.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1057  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1057) '**`_to_usd` in the worker.** RFD66606-1053. The layer records the GLB as an asset attribute, because `usd-core` alone reads no glTF. A glTF file format plugin would let it be a reference arc.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1057  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1057) '**The `idtx_core` NIF adapter.** RFD66606-1061. `flow/adapters/` in `thirdparty/fabric-flow-adapters/` holds three hosts, Godot, Unity, CLI, and no Elixir one. Needs a fourth adapter, a `weftspun_studio` route, and the browser call site swapped over. RFD66606-1061's stopgap (`prepareGlbForApiUpload` in `glbCompress.js`) stays until this lands.
 # tags: rfd:details
